            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks again for suggestion!\r\n\r\nI think I am going through with this, but want to make it more aligned with 'mini.jump2d' module by adding `allowed_lines` setting. Like this:\r\n```lua\r\n...\r\n  allowed_lines = {\r\n    cursor_before = true, -- Lines before cursor line\r\n    cursor_at = true, -- Cursor line\r\n    cursor_after = true, -- Lines after cursor line\r\n  },\r\n...\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith this, your request is covered by `cursor_before = false, cursor_after = false`.\r\n\r\nI believe this is doable by combining special `\\%<23l`, `\\%23l`, `\\%>23l` patterns to match specific lines (not `\\%<.l` and friends, because they are not present in Neovim<=0.6). This should handle both highlighting and search.\r\n\r\nI am comfortable with either implementing this myself or guiding you through. It will require implementing custom helper for dealing with this setting, as well as properly documenting and extensively testing it.",
